    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d311">

                <pb facs="0598" n="472" xml:id="pg472"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">718.1915/703</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >South</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-02-02"><hi rendition="#italic">February 2,
                        1925.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 13.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 628</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s telegram No.
                    10 of January 23, 4 p.m., and confirming my telegram No. 13 of January 30, 11
                        a.m.,<anchor n="24" xml:id="d311-f1"/> I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    a copy of a note dated January 29, 1925 from the Minister for Foreign Affairs,
                    in which is set forth the attitude of the Panaman Government with regard to the
                    settlement of the Costa Rica boundary question. A translation of the above note
                    is also inclosed.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>This morning I received a note dated January 30, 1925, a copy and translation of
                    which are enclosed, informing me that the Government of Panama considers it
                    essential that some agreement along the lines specified in the communication of
                    January 29th be reached, before Panama can name its engineer to proceed with the
                    demarcation of the boundary line.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. G. South</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d311-a1.xml" xpointer="d311-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d311-a2.xml" xpointer="d311-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
